    {
      "type": "Feature",
      "properties": {
        "project_name": "Crescent Cove",
        "site": "Mission Bay North",
        "status": "complete",
        "use": "residential",
        "geometry_type": "real",
        "digitized_from": "DataSF Assessor parcels (acdm-wktn), lot 8703006 (mapped 2005-07-28; active); the earlier outline came from: DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8703006); name/address from OpenStreetMap way 288672372 (420 Berry St)",
        "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-19 for Mission Bay's third real-buildings pass (remaining uncovered footprints inside the official Mission Bay North/South redevelopment-area boundary): Crescent Cove, a 236-unit affordable apartment complex (up to 60% AMI) at 420 Berry St next to Mission Creek Park, developed by Related Companies and Chinatown Community Development Center, designed by David Baker & Associates to follow the curve of the Caltrain tracks; sold to a SoCal investor in 2022 per The Real Deal, which places its original completion in the 2000s (exact year not independently confirmed). 2026-09-29 accuracy audit: the 'original completion in the 2000s (exact year not independently confirmed)' wording is stale: The Real Deal says Related and the Chinatown CDC 'developed Crescent Cove in 2007', David Baker Architects' project page says 'Completed 2007', and DBI permit 200505112108 completed 2007-10-30. REPLACED 2026-10-12 (shape; status and use unchanged): the owner approved building records whose outline matches an Assessor lot at 85% or better, both ways, using the lot (CLAUDE.md, 'An official parcel beats our drawing'). DataSF's Assessor layer (data/raw/parcels.geojson) has Assessor lot 8703006 (14,408 m2, active, mapped 2005-07-28); the earlier outline of 3,874 m2 and the lot overlap with IoU 0.27 (100% of the earlier outline lies inside the lot and it covers 27% of the lot). The outline is now that lot using the lots' own vertices (no simplification). geometry_type stays 'real'. Previous digitized_from: 'DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8703006); name/address from OpenStreetMap way 288672372 (420 Berry St)'. Previous accuracy_caveat: 'REAL -- surveyed DataSF Building Footprints outline (mblr SF8703006), cross-referenced by position against an OpenStreetMap building/address point (way 288672372) for the name and street address; not a hand trace or plan estimate. Completed 2007 per David Baker Architects' project page and The Real Deal; DBI permit 200505112108 shows completed 2007-10-30 (the Assessor year built is also 2007).'.",
        "accuracy_caveat": "REAL lot geometry -- the outline is Assessor lot 8703006 (14,408 m2, active), so its edges are recorded lot lines, not a surveyed building footprint: it includes any yard, setback or plaza inside the lot and can sit a little off the walls. Until 2026-10-12 this record showed the surveyed building footprint (DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8703006)); 100% of that outline lies inside the lot and it covered 27% of the lot. The lot is about 3.7 times the building footprint's area (14,408 m2 against 3,874 m2) and extends well beyond the building, including along the freeway ramps to the north-east.",
        "notes": "Completed 2007 per David Baker Architects' project page and The Real Deal; DBI permit 200505112108 completed 2007-10-30.",
        "source_doc_urls": [
          "https://therealdeal.com/sanfrancisco/2022/05/31/socal-investor-buys-236-unit-affordable-complex-in-sfs-mission-bay/",
          "https://www.dbarchitect.com/projects/crescent-cove",
          "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/288672372"
        ]
